  "body": "podliner v2.1.0\n\nfeeds now refresh on their own (#32), and mpris finally says what is playing (#33).\n\n## new\n\n- **feeds are fetched on start and every 60 minutes.** before, nothing was fetched until you typed `:refresh`, so a library could sit on old episodes for months. the sidebar title shows how old the feeds are (`Feeds · 12m ago`, `Feeds · refreshing`, `Feeds · 2 failed`). change the interval with `:refresh auto <minutes>`, turn it off with `:refresh auto off` or `RefreshIntervalMinutes: 0`. `--offline` fetches nothing.\n\n## fixed\n\n- **mpris metadata was always empty** and a paused episode showed as stopped. it read the current episode from a field nothing ever set. title, show, length and track id now come through, so waybar, playerctl and the gnome/kde widgets show the episode.\n- **no audio engine installed** crashed with an unhandled exception and a stack trace. podliner now says to install vlc, mpv or ffmpeg, with the pacman, apt and brew line, and exits.\n- **the first key after resizing the terminal was lost** or came out as garbage.\n- **a refresh moved the selection back to the first episode.** with refreshes running on their own that would have pulled the cursor away while you browse.\n- **`--offline` and `:net offline` lasted about a second**: the next network check switched back online. going offline by hand now holds until `:net online`.\n- **`--log-dir` was ignored under systemd**, logs went to the journal instead.\n- the help and readme said `g` / `G` jump to the top and bottom of the list. they seek to the start and end of the episode.\n\n## under the hood\n\n- new smoke tests in a real pty: auto refresh against a local feed server that counts requests, typing right after a resize, and starting with no audio engine.\n"
